[00:07.48]Ev’ry newborn child, Ev’ry drop of rain,
[00:14.49]Ev’ry golden ray of sun, Each head of grain—
[00:21.76]All are gifts from God; They reveal his way.
[00:29.00]Miracles performed by him sustain us each day.
[00:35.13](Chorus)
[00:35.28]So, what are we to do with a gift so rare
[00:42.66]But to love the One who gave it and show him we care.
[00:50.02]No matter what we do, We never can earn it.
[00:57.12]This gift is still a gift—The miracle of life.
[01:12.26]Others may give up, Lose their will to try,
[01:19.42]Echoing the wife of Job: “Curse God and die.”
[01:26.24]We are not that way; Praise to God we give,
[01:33.84]Thanking him for ev’ry precious moment we live.
[01:40.29](Chorus)
[01:40.44]So, what are we to do with a gift so rare
[01:47.08]But to love the ones around us and show them we care.
[01:54.80]No matter what we do, We never can earn it.
[02:01.89]This gift is still a gift—The miracle of life.
